    "recommendations": "• Trim vegetation along the access drive to maintain clear passage for emergency vehicles along the full length of the driveway.\n• Cut back dense vegetation near the detached structure to keep a clear path between the main residence and detached structure for responder movement.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers or posts visible from the road in both directions.\n• Keep any gates in fenced sections unlocked or install a knox box or standard responder lock to allow immediate access without delay.\n• Clear a staging area near the front entry that is free of parked vehicles, equipment, or landscaping features so responders have an unobstructed work area close to the main entrance.\n• Mark or identify the rear access point so responders arriving from the front can quickly locate the route to the back of the property.\n• Trim shrubs and low tree branches along walkways connecting the main residence and detached structure so responders can move between structures without obstruction.\n• Post the property address visibly at both the road entrance and the front entry of the main residence."
